From b08d0f2547962b64518b557d72d849db8c62f985 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:10:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: isolate child startup image identity from the session

Keep unpublished image and module state in the starting thread_data, keyed by its PEB, including failed startups. Avoid lazily allocated Darwin TLV state in fault-handler readers. Read WoW64 identity and CPU-area machine from the target owner; native TEBs inherit the creator PEB. Paired window-backed TEB/PEB allocation remains pending the suballocator.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-03-portal2-wine-window.md
Offered-upstream: no
